{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1403154-alternate-universes-where-each-of-the-different-traditions-paradigms-become-dominant","id":1403154,"title":"alternate universes where each of the different Traditions Paradigms become dominant?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-16T14:27:43-07:00","id":1403154,"title":"alternate universes where each of the different Traditions Paradigms become dominant?","content":"In the Mage Storytellers guide theirs one called the The Biscocchian Coprosperity Sphere.<br /> <br /> Where some random mage had Gutenberg print a copy of Kitab al-Alacir, which lead to Either ideas spreading like wildfire.<br /> <br /> Reddit user mathemagics15 discusses what would happen in a OOH world Now I'm imagining an entire planet ruled by wizard-lords, where Hermetic Magic has essentially overtaken the role technology has in our own world.<br /> <br /> Students in schools are not shown the periodic table when learning about Physics, but instead study things like the four (or five) elements, alchemy, the anatomy of the soul (avatars, chakras, you name it) and so on.<br /> <br /> Due to the nature of the Hermetic dominance, so much conventional magic has become hardcoded in consensus that most ordinary mortals can become sorcerers and perform linear magic as readily as people today can operate machines and computers. Alchemy, summoning rituals to interact with spirits and demons, the trapping of genies in bottles and lamps, the crafting of wards, fetishes and other magical items using rare and potently magical ingredients or creating them at a ley line / under a full moon... all of that doesn't actually take Awakened Will to do.<br /> <br /> Nations are led by councils of powerful willworkers, and wars are fought by summoning mythic beasts and nuking cities with magical artillery (Hermetics are experts of the Forces after all). Each nation has a Dragon air force or something similar, and international shipping still occurs by sail. Greatly sped up, however, by having water mystics calm the waves and storm mages calibrate the wind.<br /> The world is still divided culturally, and religion probably still exists, but divisions of culture and religion are intimately tied to differences in how each culture views magic. Say, the soul might be a point of contention.<br /> <br /> Natural disasters and big arcane accidents are pretty common with all the elemental magic being worked, and the population is inclined to believe that a Hermetic with enough power, knowledge, preparation and magical paraphernalia can do nearly anything.<br /> <br /> Which leads to a sad affair where the majority of the human population is controlled by conclaves of mega-powerful sorcerers and possibly even spirits, and resistance is difficult without, say, making pacts with demons or wyrm spirits or whatever to cause revolution by entropy.<br /> <br /> I don't think I would want to live under Hermetic rule","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T16:02:51-07:00","id":1403160,"title":"","content":"I wouldn\u2019t either, but it\u2019s a cool campaign setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T19:32:56-07:00","id":1403171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1403154-alternate-universes-where-each-of-the-different-traditions-paradigms-become-dominant#post1403154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think I would want to live under Hermetic rule</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither would I, but I also would not want to live in a world run by the Verbena, the Euthanatos, or the Chorus. A Sahajiya world would probably have little pleasure to it, and an Etherite world would still wallow in phrenology and eugenics. Not that that Brotherhood, the Dreamspeakers [edit] would be much better[edit], and the Adepts would be smacking people in the face with ban hammers in the real world. Really, any of the worlds they are all after would be misery, unless you had a lot of power and were a part of the system/establishment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 07-17-2020, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T20:19:47-07:00","id":1403174,"title":"","content":"A Dreamspeaker one would be ... interesting. Basically a world in which the concept of animism is a universally accepted objective fact and every object, location, animal, and even concepts are recognized as having a spiritual aspect which may or may not be fully awakened (in the normal sense of the word) and aware. This would require a lot of social rules and rituals of proper spiritual etiquette and methods of negotiation, appeasement and offerings. And it doesn't necessarily result in a preindustrial technology level either. Technological and economic development would involve taking into account the spiritual impact of development, as would warfare, exploration, and colonization. The modern world would probably be very Asian in certain ways, with certain aspects of Shintoism or the use of Feng Shui as two examples being prevalent around the world, but taking into account cultural lenses such as the angelic hosts, djinn, ancestor spirits, and the like. Naturally, some spirits are inherently hostile to human beings, and will need to be reigned in and guarded agents by some sort of elite force. There's probably a number of anime series and other East Asian media one could draw on for inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T00:16:50-07:00","id":1403190,"title":"","content":"There's a fantasy book series, the Legend of Eli Monpress, that strikes me as a pretty cool example of what a Dreamspeaker based setting might look like. It did a lot of interesting things with the idea of everything having a spirit that can be perceived and interacted with, by a select group of people. It's not a setting I'd particularly want to live in, but it would definitely make for a fun game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T02:16:21-07:00","id":1403197,"title":"","content":"It's more interesting if the world is dominated by the traditions, but not by a tradition. So that the paradigm noticably shifts depending on where you are. You have countries in Europe where the Hermetics rule, but there are others where the Celestial Chorus or the Verbana rule. While in the East you countries ruled by Dreamspeakers or Akashic Brotherhood and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T02:30:03-07:00","id":1403198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1403154-alternate-universes-where-each-of-the-different-traditions-paradigms-become-dominant?p=1403174#post1403174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Dreamspeaker one would be ... interesting. Basically a world in which the concept of animism is a universally accepted objective fact and every object, location, animal, and even concepts are recognized as having a spiritual aspect which may or may not be fully awakened (in the normal sense of the word) and aware. This would require a lot of social rules and rituals of proper spiritual etiquette and methods of negotiation, appeasement and offerings. And it doesn't necessarily result in a preindustrial technology level either. Technological and economic development would involve taking into account the spiritual impact of development, as would warfare, exploration, and colonization. The modern world would probably be very Asian in certain ways, with certain aspects of Shintoism or the use of Feng Shui as two examples being prevalent around the world, but taking into account cultural lenses such as the angelic hosts, djinn, ancestor spirits, and the like. Naturally, some spirits are inherently hostile to human beings, and will need to be reigned in and guarded agents by some sort of elite force. There's probably a number of anime series and other East Asian media one could draw on for inspiration.</div> </div> </div> </div>I presume that their is less monotheistic faiths?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T05:13:33-07:00","id":1403209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1403154-alternate-universes-where-each-of-the-different-traditions-paradigms-become-dominant?p=1403171#post1403171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Neither would I, but I also would not want to live in a world run by the Verbena, the Euthanatos, or the Chorus. A Sahajiya world would probably have little pleasure to it, and an Etherite world would still wallow in phrenology and eugenics. Not that that Brotherhood, the Dreamspeakers, and the Adepts would be smacking people in the face with ban hammers in the real world. Really, any of the worlds they are all after would be misery, unless you had a lot of power and were a part of the system/establishment.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Sahajiya world would be nothing but pleasure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T05:57:55-07:00","id":1403213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1403154-alternate-universes-where-each-of-the-different-traditions-paradigms-become-dominant?p=1403209#post1403209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Sahajiya world would be nothing but pleasure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even though we should remmebr that pain has a reason in our world. Too much pain is bad, sure, but imagine a world where <i>everything </i>is pleasure. Did you poisoned yourself? Pleasure. Do you cut pieces of your flesh? Pleasure. Do you kill your loved ones? Pleasure. <br /> <br /> Pleasure is terrifying, because it also means an end for empathy and reason. It is a very egoistic world, where everyone exist only for their own sake, while oracles and seers guide the drugged masses towards whatever they are meant to do. I personally don't want to live in an every lasting bacchanal, thank you very much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T06:07:07-07:00","id":1403214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1403154-alternate-universes-where-each-of-the-different-traditions-paradigms-become-dominant?p=1403213#post1403213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even though we should remmebr that pain has a reason in our world. Too much pain is bad, sure, but imagine a world where <i>everything </i>is pleasure. Did you poisoned yourself? Pleasure. Do you cut pieces of your flesh? Pleasure. Do you kill your loved ones? Pleasure. <br /> <br /> Pleasure is terrifying, because it also means an end for empathy and reason. It is a very egoistic world, where everyone exist only for their own sake, while oracles and seers guide the drugged masses towards whatever they are meant to do. I personally don't want to live in an every lasting bacchanal, thank you very much.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it\u2019s like a slaanshi cult?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T06:08:04-07:00","id":1403215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1403154-alternate-universes-where-each-of-the-different-traditions-paradigms-become-dominant?p=1403198#post1403198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I presume that their is less monotheistic faiths?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Dreamspeaker dominated world seems like it would be nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T06:27:13-07:00","id":1403219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1403154-alternate-universes-where-each-of-the-different-traditions-paradigms-become-dominant?p=1403209#post1403209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Sahajiya world would be nothing but pleasure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno about this...considering an Ecstatic Mage's Kamamarga can be any activity that they find pleasurable and worthy...You know, I'm not too big on sports (to say the least), and in the CoE Revised book there is this example character called Extreme Athlete. Consider an entire city living under his purview. A day starting with a one hour long hardcore 'warm-up' for everyone seems kind of too much. And there are also the radical Ecstatic groups. The very cover of their Revised Tradition Book has what seems to me a prideful Ecstatic,<br /> It's a point brought up very often in their Revised book, that some Ecstatics think mundane humans should be forced into (rather than eased into) greater extremes of activity and pleasure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 07-17-2020, 09:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T06:41:59-07:00","id":1403222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1403154-alternate-universes-where-each-of-the-different-traditions-paradigms-become-dominant?p=1403209#post1403209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Sahajiya world would be nothing but pleasure.</div> </div> </div> </div>What ever happens to people (sleepers and other mages), pain or pleasure, would be decided entirely by the Sahajiya. And any agency, power, and choice, would be entirely in the hands of the Sahajiya. How many crumbs and table scraps the Sahajiya would give to their dogs and pets is debatable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T07:08:30-07:00","id":1403224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1403154-alternate-universes-where-each-of-the-different-traditions-paradigms-become-dominant?p=1403222#post1403222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What ever happens to people (sleepers and other mages), pain or pleasure, would be decided entirely by the Sahajiya. And any agency, power, and choice, would be entirely in the hands of the Sahajiya. How many crumbs and table scraps the Sahajiya would give to their dogs and pets is debatable.</div> </div> </div> </div>In such a scenario, I can see &quot;This is technically legal under the Code of Ananda...&quot; being used a lot by some Ecstatic Mages to justify and enforce whatever would be their outlooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T07:51:32-07:00","id":1403231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1403154-alternate-universes-where-each-of-the-different-traditions-paradigms-become-dominant?p=1403224#post1403224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In such a scenario, I can see &quot;This is technically legal under the Code of Ananda...&quot; being used a lot by some Ecstatic Mages to justify and enforce whatever would be their outlooks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, even in the canon setting only about half the Cult cares about the Code IIRC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1410,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","user":"Czernobog","date":". 07-17-2020, 11:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T12:22:05-07:00","id":1403270,"title":"","content":"Oh<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t think about that. I thought a world governed by the ebb and flow of pleasure would be kinda fun, at least for a few weeks.<br /> <br /> Anyway<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a famous line in history my ex told me about where some dude calls Freud\u2019s work a joke and inspired him to write a book about the psychology of jokes. I\u2019m not exactly a big fan of Freud, but listening to you guys debate inspired me the same way. When I\u2019m done with Son of the Dragon imma buy CoE revised and form my own opinion on the issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25665,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 07-17-2020, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T17:06:13-07:00","id":1403305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1403154-alternate-universes-where-each-of-the-different-traditions-paradigms-become-dominant#post1403154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think I would want to live under Hermetic rule</div> </div> </div> </div>if you had to choose between our world and the Hermetic one, which one would you pick?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T18:14:49-07:00","id":1403317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1403154-alternate-universes-where-each-of-the-different-traditions-paradigms-become-dominant?p=1403198#post1403198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I presume that their is less monotheistic faiths?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. Monotheism and Animism are not automatically mutually exclusive. Christianity, for example, would see a much stronger emphasis on the existence of angels and demons. Catholic and other &quot;high church&quot; denominations would probably keep its use of Saints and theurgy, and &quot;low church&quot; groups are likely to have a strong Pentecostal influence. Both would have priests who are trained exorcists. I'm not enough of an expert on Jewish theology to say much more than that Kabbalism is probably more wide spread. <br /> You'd probably also see a number of syncretist belief systems such as some of the more Catholic oriented variations of Santeria or the Din-i Ilahi/&quot;Religion of God&quot; that the Mughal emperor Akbar tried to create in the 16th century.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-17T18:38:17-07:00","id":1403318,"title":"","content":"An Ecstatic world would probably be somewhat scary. The cornerstone of Ecstatic belief is Lakashim, the Worldpulse/Heartbeat of the Universe, and the effort to touch/experience it. Lakashim is tapped into through emotion, passion, and unconscious instinct. Intellect and rationality are a double-edged sword, blocking one's efforts to feel the Worldpulse but also being necessary to focus one's perceptions so that you can go beyond simple sensation or intellect and reach a perfect state of consciousness in tune with Lakashim. <br /> This means a world where logic and philosophy - and with it the development of a lot of the ideas the modern world has been built upon - are probably further behind than ours, possibly even stuck as an early Greek level in the West and things like Legalism or Confucianism never really developing in the East. (That's presuming you set an alt history divergence point back that far, rather than trying to come up with something sensible in a more modern period.) Religions are going to be pretty fanatical, being firmly focused on trying to invoke direct communion with the Divine via the various paths of ecstasy (kamamarga), including Pentecostal experiences (possession by the Holy Spirit and speaking in tongues), acting as Spirit Horses for Loa, drug induced vision quests, self-flagellation and other forms of self-harm, near-death experiences, Bacchanalian orgies that probably sometimes include the murderous frenzies of the Maenads, congress with demons and other spirits, and physical exertion to the point of exhaustion. But at least they're unlikely to be excessively dogmatic or totalitarian. Society is probably overrun with various sects and movements fanatically devoted to tearing down anything that tries to reign in emotion and the search for Lakashim, as well as reflexively combating any form of orthodoxy or status quo. However, on the bright side, there are also those who are focused on cultivating the simple pleasures of existence and helping others achieve joy and ecstasy through less destructive means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T04:48:11-07:00","id":1403366,"title":"","content":"Okay. So basically four people think a world run by the CoE is a really bad thing. I just saw it as an endless party. My bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T05:11:23-07:00","id":1403371,"title":"","content":"This is a cool idea for a thread! What I like is when a paradigm because dominant then it still creates divergent splinter groups like how the world became technocratic but we got archaic out there tech from Etherites and Adepts only slightly mystical but more philosophically free. Like if the world became more Akashic would the Hermetics shift a bit towards the Wu Lung, like become a house under their, while the Ecstatics would go towards their Hindu roots?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T05:28:49-07:00","id":1403374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1403154-alternate-universes-where-each-of-the-different-traditions-paradigms-become-dominant?p=1403366#post1403366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. So basically four people think a world run by the CoE is a really bad thing. I just saw it as an endless party. My bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage is part of the World of Darkness; as such, <i>any</i> group given dominance is going to go sour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T06:57:57-07:00","id":1403381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1403154-alternate-universes-where-each-of-the-different-traditions-paradigms-become-dominant?p=1403305#post1403305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> if you had to choose between our world and the Hermetic one, which one would you pick?</div> </div> </div> </div>This one, I\u2019ll chose this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T07:06:16-07:00","id":1403384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1403154-alternate-universes-where-each-of-the-different-traditions-paradigms-become-dominant?p=1403374#post1403374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mage is part of the World of Darkness; as such, <i>any</i> group given dominance is going to go sour.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T11:37:12-07:00","id":1403405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1403154-alternate-universes-where-each-of-the-different-traditions-paradigms-become-dominant?p=1403366#post1403366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. So basically four people think a world run by the CoE is a really bad thing. I just saw it as an endless party. My bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, it is an endless party, or at least a series of endless parties. It's just that some peoples' idea of a party - Hollywood drug orgies, Pentecostal snake handling rituals, or the Cenobites from Clive Barker's Hellraiser - aren't going to be everyone's idea of a good time. This is one of the reasons the Code of Ananda stresses respect for others and not forcing your preferred path of ecstasy on to unwilling participants. It's a paradigm that requires one to willingly seek it out, which is probably why having it be the dominant world view would require a pretty massive shift in either human nature (the general preference for the safe and routine) or world history/civilization development. <br /> Just personally, I tend to divide the Cult into four types based on general kamamarga/paths of ecstasy. The Bringers of Joy (happiness and pleasure) would be the most common, and easiest for &quot;normal&quot; people to get behind. The Seekers of the Divine (religious faith and divine congress) and Sowers of Discord (rejection of orthodoxy and routine) would require a bit more dedication and devotion. The Destroyers of Flesh (annihilation of the self and extreme tribulation) are going to be fanatical outliers no matter what. <br /> <br /> (I keep thinking it would be interesting to have an Ecstatic sect based entirely on the simple pleasures of work and craft. The sort of people who lose themselves &quot;in the now&quot; of cooking, gardening, making furniture, and the like.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T12:16:17-07:00","id":1403407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1403154-alternate-universes-where-each-of-the-different-traditions-paradigms-become-dominant?p=1403405#post1403405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, it is an endless party, or at least a series of endless parties. It's just that some peoples' idea of a party - Hollywood drug orgies, Pentecostal snake handling rituals, or the Cenobites from Clive Barker's Hellraiser - aren't going to be everyone's idea of a good time. This is one of the reasons the Code of Ananda stresses respect for others and not forcing your preferred path of ecstasy on to unwilling participants.</div> </div> </div> </div>The same code of Ananda that about half the Cult of Ecstasy canonically thinks is for losers, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's a paradigm that requires one to willingly seek it out, which is probably why having it be the dominant world view would require a pretty massive shift in either human nature (the general preference for the safe and routine) or world history/civilization development </div> </div> </div>Indeed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (I keep thinking it would be interesting to have an Ecstatic sect based entirely on the simple pleasures of work and craft. The sort of people who lose themselves &quot;in the now&quot; of cooking, gardening, making furniture, and the like.) </div> </div> </div>That would be interesting, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1410,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","user":"Czernobog","date":". 07-18-2020, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T14:39:23-07:00","id":1403419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1403154-alternate-universes-where-each-of-the-different-traditions-paradigms-become-dominant?p=1403405#post1403405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> . . .<br /> <br /> (I keep thinking it would be interesting to have an Ecstatic sect based entirely on the simple pleasures of work and craft. The sort of people who lose themselves &quot;in the now&quot; of cooking, gardening, making furniture, and the like.)</div> </div> </div> </div>We could call them the 'Domestic Sensualists,' since Kraftwerks is taken by the night-club kids. This group has connections to House Jerbiton and House Veriditus in the Order of Hermes and the Society (Sons if you prefer) of Ether. They aren't into the perfection of crafts for the sake of power or making crazy magic like the Order of Hermes, or to so many of the crazy theories of the Society of Ether, though they respect the attention to individual excellence in crafting. House Jerbiton, now a diminished house in the Order of Hermes, was about creating art and beauty.<br /> <br /> So, while the practical craftwork of the Domestic Sensualists might not agree with House Jerbiton's aesthetics, when something practical and beautiful is made, both groups are happy. The Domestic Sensualists probably draw members from various arts-and-crafts revival movements throughout history and are the type who, wherever they are making something, it's joyous to behold.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T19:06:39-07:00","id":1403461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1403154-alternate-universes-where-each-of-the-different-traditions-paradigms-become-dominant?p=1403405#post1403405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, it is an endless party, or at least a series of endless parties. It's just that some peoples' idea of a party - Hollywood drug orgies, Pentecostal snake handling rituals, or the Cenobites from Clive Barker's Hellraiser - aren't going to be everyone's idea of a good time. This is one of the reasons the Code of Ananda stresses respect for others and not forcing your preferred path of ecstasy on to unwilling participants. It's a paradigm that requires one to willingly seek it out, which is probably why having it be the dominant world view would require a pretty massive shift in either human nature (the general preference for the safe and routine) or world history/civilization development. <br /> Just personally, I tend to divide the Cult into four types based on general kamamarga/paths of ecstasy. The Bringers of Joy (happiness and pleasure) would be the most common, and easiest for &amp;quot;normal&amp;quot; people to get behind. The Seekers of the Divine (religious faith and divine congress) and Sowers of Discord (rejection of orthodoxy and routine) would require a bit more dedication and devotion. The Destroyers of Flesh (annihilation of the self and extreme tribulation) are going to be fanatical outliers no matter what. <br /> <br /> (I keep thinking it would be interesting to have an Ecstatic sect based entirely on the simple pleasures of work and craft. The sort of people who lose themselves &amp;quot;in the now&amp;quot; of cooking, gardening, making furniture, and the like.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s really useful. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T14:26:36-07:00","id":1403571,"title":"","content":"My further thoughts on the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1360544-homebrew-headcanons?p=1403570#post1403570\">Cult of Ecstasy and their various factions here</a>.<br /> <br /> Also currently pondering two different Celestial Chorus ideas, one based on ancient Egypt and the other on the Middle Ages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 07-19-2020, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T07:58:30-07:00","id":1404023,"title":"","content":"Virtual adepts: haven't really been round long enough to make that big of a difference. <br /> <br /> Hermetics: Hermetic alchemy gave birth to modern science, So If Hermetic philosophy was more dominant I can only barrier to having everything better than it is now is that hermetics tended to hoard secret knowledge and didn't share information until much later (but they're still kinda secretive) 5/5 stars. <br /> <br /> Etherites: The Good: That Renaissance was a real renaissance and a half, and we'd have those elusive hoverboards we've always wanted. The bad news is that computers would suck and we'd have probably destroyed the earth. 4/5<br /> <br /> Every other tradition: Technological advancement would stagnate during the medieval period. Also I'd feel we'd tire of certain viewpoints. 1/5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T19:02:43-07:00","id":1404152,"title":"","content":"Great, now I want to write up an alternate timeline where King Suleiman lost the War of Enslavement thanks to large factions of human Mages siding with the Djinn. This, in turn, fosters healthier, more equitable human-spirit relationships. Umbral practices remain fairly reliable and easy to do, and spirits and humans help eachother well enough that there is no pressing need for the Order of Reason or Council of Traditions to come into existence. Instead, the practices develop along more Umbra-oriented lines, and the largest unified body is made up of various spirit mages who maintain travel and diplomatic relationships between humans and various classes of spirit, divided by the entities they specialize in invoking and interacting with. There would be ersatz Choristers who work with angels, ersatz Void Engineers/Etherites who work with aliens, ersatz Hermetics/Taftani who work with djinn, and of course the most respected of all, the venerable alliance of ancient shamans who deal with nature spirits: the Dreamspeakers.<br /> <br /> I will grant, it's hardly an especially <i>Dark </i>world, but I think it would be a fun one to run games in...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-09T22:11:33-07:00","id":1407234,"title":"","content":"Hermetics would probably not be like ours. For starters, from what I remember, Hermetics are *not* happy with sharing out their knowledge. They're a mystery cult. So powerful overlords, people who are in the lower level of hierarchy having linear sorcery, and with peasants at the bottom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T16:09:55-07:00","id":1408274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1403154-alternate-universes-where-each-of-the-different-traditions-paradigms-become-dominant?p=1407234#post1407234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hermetics would probably not be like ours. For starters, from what I remember, Hermetics are *not* happy with sharing out their knowledge. They're a mystery cult. So powerful overlords, people who are in the lower level of hierarchy having linear sorcery, and with peasants at the bottom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. A divergence point revolving around the early machinations of Tremere and his inner circle, in this case their plot to frame House Diedne as Infernalists gets discovered and the Tremere are ultimately purged around 1000AD instead of Diedne. Because of this, there is no Wizards' March against the Tremere at the start of the 13th century, and when the Craftmasons try to siege Mistridge in 1210, the defenses hold and the artificers are routed. Because this attack isn't mistaken as an attack by the (non-existent) Tremere or as just an accident of the Albigensian Crusade, the Order crushes the Craftmasons. <br /> Because the Order tends to keep itself apart from mundane politics and culture, they don't really get involved with politics or history. However, House Mercere's tasks are expanded to keeping an eye out for any more potential problems like the Craftmasons. This includes them undermining - and with the help of House Jerbiton, coopting - much of the power of the High Guild, and House Verditius absorbing a number of Greek artificers fleeing the falling Byzantine empire. Meanwhile, House Diedne and Bjornaer have absorbed many of the former Old Faith under their banner. <br /> The main potential threats to the Order at this point are the Gabrielites, who have by now mostly corrected/destroyed the Messianic Voices, and the Web of Faith in the Islamic world. <br /> <br /> I'm not sure where it would go from there. I sort of have a vague idea in my head of a world that stopped at Renaissance or Enlightenment level technology but is augmented with ritual magic/alchemy into a sort of rapiers &amp; airships style fantasy setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T01:37:29-07:00","id":1408322,"title":"","content":"I think that a member of the technocracy or at least the order of reason can arise in a hermetic controlled world.<br /> <br /> Just make it so that they're a bunch of people who've 'discovered' that most of the complicated rituals are just dross set up to confuse the common man and have made it their mission to simplify it for everyday use.<br /> <br /> I'm more interested in an Akashic world. Technocracy would be those guys using giant robot suits rebelling against super martial artists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T20:08:02-07:00","id":1408443,"title":"","content":"I suppose the Virtual Adept world would be humanity uploaded into the Digital Web into something akin to the more interesting aspects of The Matrix and Ready Player One.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T20:16:34-07:00","id":1408445,"title":"","content":"You know how <b>Adventure!</b> could be thought of as \u201cwhat if the Sons of Ether won the Ascension War?\u201d Well, there's this <i>other</i> game that can be thought of as \u201cwhat if the Virtual Adepts won the Ascension War?\u201d And that would be <b>Eclipse Phase</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T00:52:40-07:00","id":1409090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1403154-alternate-universes-where-each-of-the-different-traditions-paradigms-become-dominant?p=1408274#post1408274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm. A divergence point revolving around the early machinations of Tremere and his inner circle, in this case their plot to frame House Diedne as Infernalists gets discovered and the Tremere are ultimately purged around 1000AD instead of Diedne. Because of this, there is no Wizards' March against the Tremere at the start of the 13th century, and when the Craftmasons try to siege Mistridge in 1210, the defenses hold and the artificers are routed. Because this attack isn't mistaken as an attack by the (non-existent) Tremere or as just an accident of the Albigensian Crusade, the Order crushes the Craftmasons. <br /> Because the Order tends to keep itself apart from mundane politics and culture, they don't really get involved with politics or history. However, House Mercere's tasks are expanded to keeping an eye out for any more potential problems like the Craftmasons. This includes them undermining - and with the help of House Jerbiton, coopting - much of the power of the High Guild, and House Verditius absorbing a number of Greek artificers fleeing the falling Byzantine empire. Meanwhile, House Diedne and Bjornaer have absorbed many of the former Old Faith under their banner. <br /> The main potential threats to the Order at this point are the Gabrielites, who have by now mostly corrected/destroyed the Messianic Voices, and the Web of Faith in the Islamic world. <br /> <br /> I'm not sure where it would go from there. I sort of have a vague idea in my head of a world that stopped at Renaissance or Enlightenment level technology but is augmented with ritual magic/alchemy into a sort of rapiers &amp; airships style fantasy setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds very cool. Would love to play in that setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-19T23:41:08-08:00","id":1425095,"title":"","content":"I RAN A post apocalyptic game with the technocracy being wiped out. the void engineers and virtual adepts folded into the etherites and basically they went out the door and into the umbra for the most part.<br /> <br /> the traditions had run of the world again and were united enough after the nephandi orchestrated apocalypse hit (which actually came back to bite them in the ass as the void they unleashed upon the world came to consume them as well, they unleashed the dark masters or anti oracles upon the earth and it destroyed them when they couldn't destabilize reality enough to destroy it completely) essentially the council of nine became the greatest world power, though many nephandi survived and continue to terrorize reality and the problems of mages are many.<br /> <br /> Now, the region of the pacific north west is under the rule of the hermetic masters of greylocke chantry (see NWO revised), as well as various dream speakers in the area, they have a peaceful relationship and there are also some other mages in the area, mostly choristers.<br /> <br /> the rest of the world isn't fleshed out so much but I decided that the traditional strongholds remained viable for many of the traditions.<br /> <br /> oh, and the Ahli'Batin came back when the digital web was shattered and reclaimed it as their mount Khaf/web of faith and thus became a super power of the traditions as they were not hit by the death of many of their great masters by the avatar storm and thus reclaimed their seat on the council and evolved into a new and powerful tradition","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-20T21:51:07-08:00","id":1425315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1403154-alternate-universes-where-each-of-the-different-traditions-paradigms-become-dominant?p=1408443#post1408443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose the Virtual Adept world would be humanity uploaded into the Digital Web into something akin to the more interesting aspects of The Matrix and Ready Player One.</div> </div> </div> </div>.... where would that leave everyone else, though? What are the tenets of the Virtual adepts, anyway? Information wants to be free, connectivity everywhere, L33T hackers, able to change reality using hacking and coding.. what else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}